# text_id = 1584
# text = He contended that there were too many Irish recruits ; and he found from a Return issued by the Quartermaster that whereas , in 1869 , there were 1,403 recruits in Ireland , the average number for the next five years was 2,250 , and for the following five years , from 1874 to 1879 , it was 3,260 .
