# text_id = 1697
# text = Mr. Fawcett said that in 1879 £ 2,800,000 drawn from India was paid in England for the purpose of pension allowances , but the sum was now £ 3,787,124 — that was to say , in the course of 10 years the amount of Indian Revenue paid in England had been increased by something very nearly approaching to £ 1,000,000 sterling .
