# text = THE PRESIDENT OF THE BOARD OF TRADE ( Sir MICHAEL HICKS - BEACH ) ( Bristol W. ) said , that the assent of the Government was confined to the Bill as it stood , because it appeared to be a useful extension of the powers under the Act of 1882 , and might , perhaps , tend to public advantage .
