# text = Beyond the questions of the existence of distress , the amendment of the Land Act , and the state of the magistracy , there were others which were urgent and pressing — for instance , the question of County Government Boards and Provincial Councils , in regard to which Ulster was in complete and full accord with the other three Provinces .
