# text_id = 1748
# text = Lord Carnarvon was particularly emphatic in July , 1885 , in quoting the well - known dictum of Cavour , which said that to conduct government permanently on the principles of a state of siege was utterly impossible , and , therefore , that it was equally impossible to govern Ireland by coercion if it was to be indefinitely re-enacted .
