# text_id = 1756
# text = It was , of course , perfectly clear that Parliament had a right to make laws ; but it had not the power to explain them after they had been made , and certainly no one branch , either the Crown , or the Lords , or the Commons , had the power of explaining Acts passed by those Estates .
