# text_id = 1761
# text = The plain English of that is that where deer forests were for the benefit of the community at large — of crofters and cottars alike — there , and there only , should the deer forest cease to be subject to the provisions of this Act , which provided that land should be taken compulsorily for the extension of holdings .
