# text_id = 1783
# text = The evil of putting Scotch affairs into the hands of Departments administered in London , was that they seemed of much less importance in the eyes of the Department than English matters ; and , being less understood by them , they were either neglected or postponed for English matters , or were bungled by being forced into English moulds .
