# text_id = 1820
# text = I wish to ask whether it is at the instance or with the consent of the Irish Executive that the Magistrates continue to apply the glaring anomaly of the jurisdiction conferred by the Statute of Edward III . in the case of a distinguished public man for the purpose of inflicting an additional sentence to that imposed under the Crimes Act ?
