# text_id = 1846
# text = The right hon . Gentleman the Chief Secretary for Ireland had stated the other day that when Irish Members used the word " respectable " with reference to some persons in Ireland they did so in a sense not used in that House — that was to say , that they did not mean trustworthy and respectable men whose words were to be relied upon , but successful men of business .
