# text_id = 1847
# text = He would refer their Lordships to the case of a man who , having bought 600 acres in the Landed Estates Court , found , on the expiration of the lease of a middleman , a sub - tenant who neither had ability to farm properly nor was able to pay a fair rent , but who yet would obtain by the Bill perpetuity or " durability " of tenure .
