# text_id = 1848
# text = MR. MACLIVER asked the Postmaster General , If his attention has been called to the reports in various newspapers , to the effect that the telegraph clerks are dissatisfied with the interview which their delegates have had with him ; and , whether , after hearing their grievances , he is prepared to remedy them , in accordance with the recommendations of influential memorialists from all parts of the United Kingdom ?
