# text = Then they had the First Naval Lord of the Admiralty ( Sir Arthur Hood ) , a man who was more directly responsible than any other individual in this matter , stating that he would be quite satisfied with the existing state of the Navy , if we laid down battle ships to take the place of those which had become obsolete , and if we gave him six additional cruisers .
