# text_id = 1872
# text = The guns often were not heard , and in fogs the rockets were not seen ; and , in many cases , they did not indicate the position of the wreck — a matter of the highest importance — nor did they give any information as to its size , or the number of passengers to be saved ; whereas the telegraph could at once communicate all these particulars .
