# text_id = 1876
# text = He felt it his duty to support in the Division Lobby the Amendment of his hon . Friend ; and he trusted that many Liberals , who claimed to be really so , would go with him , and also that many Tories , acting on principle — for they could act on principle quite as well as Liberals — would give their support to the demand of the Irish Members .
