# text_id = 1879
# text = He ( Mr. Duckham ) said the farmers of England had borne their burdens and what they felt their wrongs patiently ; they had not been violent in their demands , and they now trusted that their appeal for better regulations , whereby their property would not be wasted , and whereby the excessive burdens under which they laboured would be relieved , would not be made in vain .
