# text_id = 1884
# text = In many parts of Ireland , a tenant was accustomed to pay a year 's rent after harvest ; and if there was a hanging gale on the estate , the tenant in October , 1882 , by paying a year 's rent , as usual , would be clear up to his hanging gale , and , therefore , there would really be no arrear upon his holding .
