# text_id = 1887
# text = At any rate , they had been placed in the hands of the troops for use , and it would appear , from the explanation of the hon . Gentleman , that bayonets had been allowed to be in the hands of a regiment for 30 years without having been returned , in order to ascertain whether they were perfect , or whether any reliance could be placed upon them .
