# text_id = 1889
# text = He ( Mr. Chamberlain ) thought he was right in saying that , in one debate on the Land Act of 1881 , the hon . Member went so far as to say , for himself and his Friends , that the state of certain districts in Ireland was such that he , for one , had come to the opinion that some scheme of emigration would be worth trying .
