# text_id = 1890
# text = He called it most insulting — first , because , for the first time , such a Bill was to be a permanent measure , and that in the teeth of the opposition of the great bulk both of the Irish Members and of the Liberal Party ; and , secondly , because of the offensive proposal to replace the trial of Irishmen by their peers by trial in England .
