# text_id = 1891
# text = As a general rule , the privilege of cutting heather or grass is not conferred as a matter of right upon the crofter , but with the assent of owner ; and , as a rule , something in the shape of rent or acknowledgment is paid , not to the owner of the land , but to the person from whose holding the grass or heather is taken .
