# text_id = 1893
# text = During the Famine of 1845 – 6 – 7 many in - stances were known in which the rates largely exceeded the value of the rateable property in the Unions ; and if the people in the Unions were driven bank upon the rates the same thing must happen now as happened then , and the rates would amount to such an enormous sum as would be impossible to pay them .
