# text_id = 1897
# text = Whatever may have been the germs from which , in remote antiquity , the first developments were made towards national unity , all that we now understand by local government was the direct work of Parliament — work performed not for the purpose of politically educating the country , but of getting some part of its business done in the way most congenial to its settled character and habits .
