# text_id = 1903
# text = He ( Mr. Gorst ) believed the meaning of the word " entertainment " had been settled by legal decisions ; and anything in the nature of a definition being now introduced into the Act would primâ facie raise the probability that the legal definition was to be altered , that the present reading was obsolete , and that some new meaning was to be attached to the term .
