# text_id = 1909
# text = COLONEL LAURIE ( Bath ) asked the First Lord of the Admiralty , Whether the Government have under their consideration a scheme for placing the Coastguard and Lifeboat Stations of the United Kingdom in direct telegraphic communication , with a view to more prompt assistance to vessels in distress and the saving of life ; and whether the lighthouses along and off the coast could be included in the scheme ?
