# text_id = 1910
# text = LORD SUDELEY said , he would not attempt to follow the noble Earl through his detailed analysis of the Return ; but he thought it would , perhaps , have been fairer not merely to have stated that only seven out of 90 Companies were carrying out the recommendations of the Board of Trade , but to have shown the number of carriages and engines fitted with continuous brakes .
