# text_id = 1920
# text = It was that the government was taken out of the hands of the constituency — out of the hands of the people as a whole — and placed in the hands of a small portion of the people — which represented not the nation as a body , but that part of it which was , for political purposes , able to spend most money in corrupting the constituencies .
