# text_id = 1924
# text = He did not know how the right hon . Gentleman , consistently with the large and liberal principles he had laid down during the second reading of the measure , was justified in deliberately proposing an arrangement which undoubtedly was calculated to produce this consequence — that in a certain number of cases the County Councils would not , at certain times , reflect the complete public opinion of the county .
