# text_id = 1928
# text = In answer to my hon . Friend 's Question on the Paper , I have to say that the Rule existing before the present Rule was brought into operation enabled any hon . Member to object to a measure being taken after half - past 12 , and that objection could be taken by simply putting a Notice on the Paper , without requiring the Member 's personal attendance .
