# text_id = 1929
# text = The hon . Member who had just intervened without reason ( Mr. H. Samuelson ) was , to a certain extent , justified by the action of the right hon . and learned Gentleman , and it was doubtless owing to a truly Liberal tenderness for the conduct of his Chiefs that he had not risen to Order during the speech of the right hon . and learned Gentleman .
