# text_id = 1930
# text = THE EARL OF REDESDALE ( CHAIRMAN of COMMITTEES ) said , he hoped it was not intended to go on with the Bill this Session , when there were scarcely any Peers on the Opposition side , and no Peer of legal knowledge remaining to critize such an important subject as a change in the Law of Libel , or to inform the House what the Bill proposed to do .
