# text_id = 1932
# text = All their Lordships were , no doubt , equally anxious to promote morality ; but the question was whether , in the attempt to do so , they were not about to legislate in a direction , and to a degree , beyond that which public opinion would sanction , and thereby to cause a reaction against their legislation which would be positively injurious to the morality they desired to promote .
