# text_id = 1933
# text = CAPTAIN AYLMER said , it seemed somewhat strange that the hon . Member for Hythe ( Sir Edward Watkin ) should have spoken so strongly in favour of the Bill , of its urgent necessity , and the injustice that would be done to the promoters by rejecting it , when it was well known that the hon . Member had been for many years an opponent of this very line .
