# text_id = 1943
# text = Why was the Local Government Board in England so careful to protect the health of the people by prohibiting the sale of this diseased meat , while the authority in Ireland — whether of Dublin Castle or the Local Government Board made little difference , for they happened to be represented by the same individual acting in a double capacity — sanctioned and encouraged this practice unknown in England ?
