# text_id = 1950
# text = This feeling was not confined to the poor people living in towns whose industry had been ruined by the disturbance of the country , but it was growing among the solvent farmers and the struggling tradesmen ; and he had great reliance in these difficulties upon what he had never doubted — namely , the kindly warm feelings which , at bottom , were in the hearts of the Irish people .
