# text_id = 1954
# text = MR. JACOB BRIGHT , in seconding the Amendment , said , he had no wish to detain the House further than to corroborate the statement of his hon . Friend ( Mr. Armitage ) as to the overwhelming strength of opinion in Manchester in favour of the Amendment — namely , that young children under the age of 10 years should not be allowed to be employed in the streets .
