# text_id = 1956
# text = The Bill threw the bulk of power and responsibility not on the parish , which was accessible to most of the people , but on the local authority of the County Council , the body least accessible to the mass of the people ; its whole framework tended to increase the power and duties of the County Council , the membership of which must be restricted to the leisured classes .
