# text_id = 1958
# text = There could be no equality of suffrage throughout the Kingdom if a house on one side of a street happened to be in a county and enfranchised not only the occupier , but perhaps a score of persons holding each a charge of 40s. , while the same house if in a borough would , so far as the borough was concerned , confer the franchise only on the rated occupier .
