# text_id = 1961
# text = On the 9th of July , Lord Lothian wrote to the effect that every effort should be made to induce the man who stated himself to be the real offender to surrender himself to justice atonce , in order that his statement might be proved , and that if the statement of such men should be proved to be true , Matheson , of course , should be liberated .
