# text_id = 1962
# text = The Lord Lieutenant might make up his mind to seize a newspaper , on the ground of certain passages which it contained ; and he ( the Secretary of State for the Home Department ) conceived it would be sufficient , when the Lord Lieutenant made up his mind , that he should cut out the passages necessary to the seizure , and specify them as the ground of the seizure .
