# text_id = 1970
# text = They were led to suppose last year , in the correspondence between M. Léon Say and Lord Granville , that the new Treaty would be based on an amelioration of the existing Treaty ; and he thought that all commercial bodies would support him in saying that they should decline , in the interests of Free Trade , to negotiate unless they actually secured some improvement on the old tariff .
