# text_id = 1973
# text = They were either high ecclesiastics of one particular religious persuasion — and it was grossly unfair that the religious persuasion of the minority of the people alone should contribute to the officers of the Executive — or renegade patriots who had reached the Bench in Ireland ; or some swaggering officers who had distinguished themselves by cruelties towards the race which had the misfortune to be subject to British rule .
