# text_id = 1978
# text = It did seem to him ( Mr. Rylands ) , that at a time when they were called upon to pay large sums of money for the Military Services of the Crown , it was most ill - advised that they should persist in voting , year after year , a sum of £ 60,000 or £ 70,000 for a Force which was condemned by the very highest authorities .
