# text_id = 1979
# text = MR. J. W. PEASE fully agreed with the remarks of the hon . Member for Newcastle ( Mr. J. Cowen ) that the pa- tronage conferred on Members of Parliament , especially upon county Members , involved them in a great deal of trouble ; for it was generally found that when one person was pleased by an appointment a great many more were disposed to quarrel with the appointment made .
