# text_id = 1982
# text = Lord Palmerston was the first man who made it a Ministerial question ; and it so went on until the great and good Tory Administration which was overthrown in 1880 came forward and said it would be no longer responsible for moving the Adjournment , that it must be left to private Members to move the Adjournment for the Derby , if it was to he moved at all .
