# text_id = 1986
# text = Though the Irish Members did not object to the police in the slightest degree so long as they were used for legitimate purposes , they did object to them when used to maintain the landlords against the just rights of the people ; and when they saw the police absolutely used as a moans of exciting the people to a breach of law and order , they must condemn that system .
