# text_id = 1997
# text = The reason he ( Colonel Saunderson ) employed the language in the House of Commons which he had used in Ireland was because he felt bound , as an honest man , to repeat in the House that which , he had used on the other side of the Channel , and which hon . Gentlemen opposite stated that they saw the disastrous results of in the Belfast riots .
