# text_id = 2002
# text = In June , 1877 , the War Office applied to the Full Court to set aside the verdict on the ground that no such contract existed , and that the verdict was against the evidence , and the Full Court unanimously decided that no contract existed so as to entitle Mr. Thomas to prefer any claim against the Crown , and they let it to Mr. Thomas to appeal .
