# text_id = 2005
# text = There is a clause in that Bill which regulates the temporary arrangement before the new authorities are established ; but if the House should reject the whole scheme of Local Government the whole scheme of the re-adjustment of the local and imperial finance would fall to the ground at the same time , and have to be considered in succeeding years when Parliament might feel disposed to take a different view .
