# text_id = 2030
# text = If it became the habit of the House , after a Select Committee had been appointed to examine into a Bill , to review the decision of that Committee , and , on a further stage of a Bill , to review the discussion , they would take a course which would not only be highly inconvenient , but would strike a serious blow at the usefulness of Select Committees .
