# text = He did not believe that the increased charges which the Bill authorized the Great North of Scotland Railway to make would be detrimental to the agricultural interest ; and he , for one , would vote , as he always intended to do — unless there were much stronger grounds than had been shown in this case — in support of the unanimous decision of the Select Committee upstairs .
