# text_id = 2047
# text = I say nothing about the cost ; that is comparatively a trifling matter ; but of course if the defendant is required to appeal it would be necessary to employ counsel to argue legal technicalities , and that expense would be saved if the Legislature were to provide that the fiat of the Attorney General should in Ireland be equivalent to an order granted in England upon a writ of certiorari .
