# text = THE VICE PRESIDENT ( Sir WILLIAM HART DYKE ) ( Kent , Dartford ) , having elicited from the hon . Member that the first part of the Question did not refer to London alone , but referred to the country generally , said that he believed oven so there were no grounds for supposing that so large a number of children evaded the vigilance of the attendance officers .
