# text_id = 2064
# text = EARL SPENCER , in moving that the Bill be now read a second time , said , that in 1877 the Universities Act established the Universities Committee of the Privy Council , whose duty it was to consider any opposed statute framed by the University Commissioners of Oxford and Cambridge , and , if such a statute should require amendment , to return it to the Commission for alteration .
