# text_id = 2070
# text = He thought , on the contrary , that the comforts of home would give higher ideas to the labourer as to the way in which he was entitled to live , and he would be more likely to look for better treatment and better wages from the farmer , if he was given a good house , than if he was placed in a wretched hovel without ordinary comforts .
