# text_id = 2081
# text = SIR FREDERICK MILNER said , he was afraid that no kind of argument would persuade the extreme section of the Radical Party to take what many Members on the Opposition side considered to be a rational and patriotic view of the question ; and , therefore , all arguments must be addressed to the more moderate Members of the Party opposite , and what remained of the old Liberal Party .
