# text = MR. RYLANDS said , he had listened with great satisfaction to the replies of the Prime Minister to the many Questions which had been put to him , because he had in his recollection that they had had such things to deal with as secret Treaties which had been entered into by a Government of this country under conditions which necessarily hoodwinked the House of Commons and deceived the people .
