# text_id = 2086
# text = The hon . Member for Oldham ( Mr. Lyulph Stanley ) was anxious that they should not discuss the question of the housing of the poor until they had determined — first , the whole question of local burdens ; secondly , what hon . Gentlemen called the land question ; thirdly , the question of local government ; and , fourthly , the question of leasehold tenure in towns .
