# text_id = 2094
# text = The opinion was that when a tumult had reached a certain point the police were justified in firing , but the Crown Solicitor considered it was a matter of very serious consideration what provocation had been given by the police in seizing the drum ; as in the Ballina case by the seizure of the drum , so in the Mitchelstown case by the forcing of a reporter through the crowd .
