# text_id = 2101
# text = MR. JESSE COLLINGS ( Birmingham , Bordesley ) said , he wished to ask the First Lord of the Treasury , with reference to his statement that the Government desired to receive practical suggestions respecting the terrible amount of land now out of cultivation , whether he would give facilities during the present Session for the consideration of those suggestions and remedies contained in the provisions of the Small Holdings Bill ?
